{
  "title": "How the Heart Pumps: A Coordinated Cycle",
  "subject": "Human heart frontal cutaway",
  "summary": "A coordinated four-chamber heart cutaway showing how blood returns from the body to the right atrium and right ventricle, is pumped through the pulmonary artery to the lungs, returns oxygenated through the pulmonary veins to the left atrium and left ventricle, and is ejected through the aorta back to the body. The animation treats the heart as one joined pump: both atria contract together and both ventricles contract together in slowed teaching stages.",
  "mode": "illustration",
  "physics": "none",
  "sourceReading": "This is a saved animation generated with Muse Wonder and Muse Image from a user-provided heart diagram. The original reference is not distributed. The left panel shows the generated artwork.",
