    "Blue and red are conventional diagram colours for oxygen-poor and oxygen-rich blood, not direct measurements from the reference image.",
    "Valve leaflets and the routes through the lungs and body are simplified for clarity; the lungs and full body circuit are implied by vessel direction rather than drawn as separate organs.",
    "Patient orientation is preserved as patient's right on viewer's left, and the generated artwork should be checked against the reference for chamber position, vessel connections and valve placement before use.",
    "This is a slowed teaching cycle, not clinical timing, pressure, volume, or valve-motion measurement; one phase is not one complete heartbeat.",
    "The finished cutaway partly hides the aortic outlet behind the pulmonary trunk and the inferior vena cava behind the right ventricle, so those short connecting segments are mapped less confidently than the visible chambers.",
    "The artwork is AI-generated; anatomical detail has not been reviewed by a medical illustrator.",
    "The illustrated tissue changes pose using generated keyframes and motion interpolation. This is not a biomechanical model."
